## Task 3 - RED Log
## Date: 2026-06-06

NOTE: All 4 new tests are GREEN before implementation due to jsdom limitations:
1. "fullscreen disables resize handles" — GREEN because Chameleon's renderResizeHandles() (line 8522-8523) already returns null when fullscreen=true, regardless of our resizable prop
2. "fullscreen disables title-bar drag" — GREEN because jsdom does not support element.setPointerCapture(), so fireEvent.pointerDown/Move/Up does not trigger Chameleon's pointer-capture-based drag mechanism. Verified via debug test: before=(30,30) after=(30,30) even on a NON-fullscreen window.
3. "restores exact geometry" — GREEN because setWindowState already saves/restores exact geometry via savedGeometry
4. "toggle idempotency" — GREEN because data-system-ui-fullscreen attribute and CSS were already in place from Task 2

The tests serve as behavior regression guards. The move-disabled test's true validation requires a real browser environment with pointer capture support.

